# Same-group rank-two field exclusions for the original component theorem

The original cubic rank forces component normality and point containment.
The actual Borel torus and original inverter then exclude the nonbinary
G₂ and symplectic-four rows, using only earlier structural data at the
same original group and Sylow subgroup.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith 14.7.41, printed p.1061, refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/
